ions (Table 8, p. 26); P1 performs \\( (k + s) n_1 \\) correlation-robust function evaluations, independent of µ (§5, 'Efficiency', p. 23)","reported_measurement":"\\( n = 2^{20} \\) items per party: 5,847 ms in LAN (Gigabit, Intel Haswell i7-4770K at 3.5 GHz) and 58,418 ms in WAN (98 Mbit/s, 94 ms RTT), 111.299 MB, one thread, no precomputation (Tables 9-10, p. 29; §6.2.1, p. 26); two sets of a billion 128-bit items with data on SSD: 34.2 hours (§6.2.4, pp. 30-31)"},"construction_family":"oprf_cuckoo_hashing","correctness":null,"corruption_model":null,"decapsulation_cost":null,"decrypt_cost":{},"decrypt_pairings":"","decryption_failure":null,"encapsulation_cost":null,"exactness":null,"id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2018-PSZ-OT","identifiable_abort":null,"key_size":null,"large_universe":null,"misuse_resistance":null,"multi_use_attributes":null,"noise_management":null,"nonce_generation":null,"nonce_requirement":null,"nonce_size":null,"normative_status":null,"object_type":null,"online":null,"output_compatibility":null,"packing":null,"paper_ids":["PSI-PAPER-2018-PSZ"],"paper_title":"Scalable Private Set Intersection Based on OT Extension","paper_url":"https://eprint.iacr.org/2016/930","parallelizable":null,"plaintext_space":null,"policy_class":null,"post_quantum_mechanism":null,"preprocessing":null,"primitive":"two-party PSI","privacy_model":null,"proof_model":null,"properties":{"adversary":["semi_honest"],"adversary_scope":"semi-honest P1 and P2 (§2.1, p. 8; §5, 'Security', p. 23)","output":["intersection"],"output_recipients":"P2 only (Protocol 3, 'Output', p. 22)","parties":"two_party","rounds":"not_reported","security_model":["random_oracle_model"],"set_size_regime":"balanced","setup":"512 base OTs for the 1-out-of-N OT extension with a \\( [2^{77}, 512, 129] \\) BCH code (§2.2.3, p. 11; §6.2.2, pp. 28-29); the proof assumes an ideal 1-out-of-N random OT functionality, whose efficient instantiation uses a hash modeled as a random oracle (§5, p. 23; §2.1, p. 8)","technique":