PSI-PAPER-2020-ION","year":2020},{"adaptive_security":null,"api_style":null,"associated_data":null,"assumption_family":"idealized_model","assumption_id":"ASM-ROM","assumption_ids":["ASM-ROM"],"assumption_name":"Non-programmable random oracles, in the OOS OT-extension hybrid model","authors":["Benny Pinkas","Mike Rosulek","Ni Trieu","Avishay Yanai"],"base_signature":null,"block_size":null,"bootstrapping":null,"capabilities":["linear-communication"],"ciphertext_security":null,"circuit_class":null,"claim_ids":["PSI-CONTRIB-2020-PRTY-MALICIOUS-PAXOS-PSI","PSI-CONTRIB-2020-PRTY-GARBLED-CUCKOO","PSI-CONTRIB-2020-PRTY-RECEIVER-SET-SIZE-BOUND"],"client_storage":null,"communication":null,"complexity":{"communication":"\\( (\\lambda + \\log_2(n_1 n_2)) n_1 + \\ell(2.4 n_2 + 2\\lambda + \\chi) + \\lambda(2.4 n_2 + 2\\ell) \\) bits excluding base OTs; about \\( 1623n \\), \\( 1621n \\), and \\( 1602n \\) bits for \\( n = 2^{16}, 2^{20}, 2^{24} \\) with \\( \\kappa = 128 \\), \\( \\lambda = 40 \\) (Table 1, p. 21); the recommended parameters are \\( \\ell_2 = 2\\kappa \\) and \\( \\ell_1 \\) of 129 to 233 bits with codewords of 583 to 776 bits, depending on the table size m and the extraction bound \\( n' \\) (§4.4, p. 15; Figure 5, p. 16)","computation":"garbled cuckoo encoding in \\( O((d + \\lambda)^{3} + n\\lambda) \\) with \\( d \\) about \\( \\log n \\), decoding by XOR of about \\( (\\lambda + d + 2)/2 \\) positions per key (§5.1, p. 18; Figure 2, p. 9); OOS OT extension on the table positions, with AES-based hash and PRF (§7.1, p. 22)","reported_measurement":"202.04 MB; 5,598 ms (LAN), 18,621 ms (WAN1, 155 MiB/s), 40,810 ms (WAN2, 55 MiB/s) for \\( n = 2^{20} \\) and 128-bit items, one thread per party on AWS M5.large (Table 2, p. 24; §7.2, p. 23)"},"construction_family":"okvs_ot_extension","correctness":null,"corruption_model":null,"decapsulation_cost":null,"decrypt_cost":{},"decrypt_pairings":"","decryption_failure":null,"encapsulation_cost":null,"exactness":null,"id":