,"summary":"This row is the protocol of Figure 3 (p. 11) with the malicious parameters of §4.4 (pp. 15-16), as described in PSI-CONTRIB-2020-PRTY-MALICIOUS-PAXOS-PSI. The longer \\( H_1 \\) output and code bound a malicious receiver's effective set (PSI-CONTRIB-2020-PRTY-RECEIVER-SET-SIZE-BOUND), and \\( H_2 \\) outputs of \\( 2\\kappa \\) bits make collisions among a malicious sender's queries negligible. In the authors' experiments the…","supported_gates":null,"tag_size":null,"threshold_policy":null,"transform":null,"update_model":null,"verification_cost":null,"work_id":"PSI-PAPER-2020-PRTY","year":2020},{"adaptive_security":null,"api_style":null,"associated_data":null,"assumption_family":"symmetric","assumption_id":"PSI-ASSUMPTION-CODE-CORRELATION-ROBUST-HASH-IN-THE-OOS-OT-EXTENSION-HYBRID-MODEL","assumption_name":"Code-correlation-robust hash, in the OOS OT-extension hybrid model","authors":["Benny Pinkas","Mike Rosulek","Ni Trieu","Avishay Yanai"],"base_signature":null,"block_size":null,"bootstrapping":null,"capabilities":["linear-communication"],"ciphertext_security":null,"circuit_class":null,"claim_ids":["PSI-CONTRIB-2020-PRTY-MALICIOUS-PAXOS-PSI","PSI-CONTRIB-2020-PRTY-GARBLED-CUCKOO","PSI-CONTRIB-2020-PRTY-PAXOS"],"client_storage":null,"communication":null,"complexity":{"communication":"\\( (\\lambda + \\log_2(n_1 n_2)) n_1 + \\ell(2.4 n_2 + \\lambda + \\chi) \\) bits excluding base OTs, with \\( n_1, n_2 \\) the sender's and receiver's set sizes and \\( \\ell \\) the OT-extension width; about \\( 1207n \\), \\( 1268n \\), and \\( 1302n \\) bits for \\( n = 2^{16}, 2^{20}, 2^{24} \\) with \\( \\kappa = 128 \\), \\( \\lambda = 40 \\) (Table 1, p. 21); codeword length 448 to 506 bits for \\( n = 2^{12} \\) to \\( 2^{24} \\) (Figure 4, p. 15)","computation":"garbled cuckoo encoding in \\( O((d + \\lambda)^{3} + n\\lambda) \\) with \\( d \\) about \\( \\log n \\), decoding by XOR of about \\( (\\lambda + d + 2)/2 \\) positions per key (§5.1, p. 18; Figure 2, p. 9); OOS OT extension on the \\( 2.4n + d + \\lambda \\) table positions, with AES-based hash and PRF (§7.1, p. 22)","reported_measurement":"163.63 MB; 5,378 ms (LAN), 17,628 ms (WAN1, 155 MiB/s), 40,524 ms (WAN2, 55 MiB/s) for \\( n = 2^{20} \\) and 128-bit items, one thread per party on AWS M5.large (Table 2, p. 24; §7.2, p. 23)"},"construction_family":"okvs_ot_extension","correctness":null,"corruption_model":null,"decapsulation_cost":null,"decrypt_cost":{},"decrypt_pairings":"","decryption_failure":null,"encapsulation_cost":null,"exactness":null,"id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2020-PRTY-SH","identifiable_abort":null,"key_size":null,"large_universe":null,"misuse_resistance":null,"multi_use_attributes":null,"noise_management":null,"nonce_generation":null,"nonce_requirement":null,"nonce_size":null,"normative_status":null,"object_type":null,"online":null,"output_compatibility":null,"packing":null,"paper_ids":["PSI-PAPER-2020-PRTY"],"paper_title":"PSI from PaXoS: Fast, Malicious Private Set Intersection","paper_url":"https://eprint.iacr.org/2020/193","parallelizable":null,"plaintext_space":null,"policy_class":null,"post_quantum_mechanism":null,"preprocessing":null,"primitive":"two-party PSI","privacy_model":null,"proof_model":null,"properties":{"adversary":["semi_honest"],"adversary_scope":"semi-honest sender and receiver; obtained from the protocol of Figure 3 by setting \\( \\ell_1 = \\ell_2 = \\lambda + 2 \\log n \\) (§4.4, p. 15)","output":["intersection"],"output_recipients":"receiver only (Figure 1, p. 6; Figure 3, step 4, p. 11)","parties":"two_party","rounds":"not_reported","security_model":["standard_model"],"set_size_regime":"balanced","setup":"base OTs for OOS, instantiated with Naor-Pinkas OTs from libOTe (§7.1, p. 22); OOS is treated as an ideal functionality (Figure 3, p. 11); the paper states standard-model security for the semi-honest case (Appendix D, p. 33), while the proof it gives is the malicious random-oracle proof (Theorem 4, p. 10)","technique":["paxos","ot_extension"]},"quantum_security":null,"query_communication":null,"resilience":null,"response_communication":null,"robustness":null,"security_mode":"computational","security_model":"semi-honest two-party; standard model as stated in Appendix D (p. 33)","security_notion":"PSI with output to the receiver","server_model":null,"server_work":null,"setup_model":null,"signer_model":null,"signing_cost":null,"signing_rounds":null,"sizes":{},"statefulness":null,"summary":"This row is the protocol of Figure 3 (p. 11), described in PSI-CONTRIB-2020-PRTY-MALICIOUS-PAXOS-PSI, with the semi-honest parameters of §4.4 (p. 15): the shortest hash outputs that keep false matches below \\( 2^{-\\lambda} \\) and a code of minimum distance κ. The encoding is the garbled cuckoo table of PSI-CONTRIB-2020-PRTY-GARBLED-CUCKOO in its 2-core form. The authors also measure a DFS-based table (Appendix B) with \\( 2n…","supported_gates":null,"tag_size":null,"threshold_policy":null,"transform":null,"update_model":null,"verification_cost":null,"work_id":"PSI-PAPER-2020-PRTY","year":2020},{"adaptive_security":null,"api_style":null,"associated_data":null,"assumption_family":"generic","assumption_id":"PSI-ASSUMPTION-ADDITIVELY-HOMOMORPHIC-ENCRYPTION-AND-YAO-GARBLED-CIRCUITS-NO-FURTHER-ASSUMPTION-STATED-FOR-THE-TWO-PARTY-CASE","assumption_name":"Additively homomorphic encryption and Yao garbled circuits; no further assumption stated for the two-party case","authors":["Saikrishna Badrinarayanan","Peihan Miao","Srinivasan Raghuraman","Peter Rindal"],"base_signature":null,"block_size":null,"bootstrapping":null,"capabilities":["sublinear-in-set-size","no-fhe"],"ciphertext_security":null,"circuit_class":null,"claim_ids":["PSI-CONTRIB-2021-BMRR-TAHE-THRESHOLD-PSI","PSI-CONTRIB-2019-GS-AHE-THRESHOLD-PSI"],"client_storage":null,"communication":null,"complexity":{"communication":"\\( \\tilde O(T) \\) (§1.2, p. 4): the singularity test via Yao's garbled circuits costs \\( \\tilde O(k \\cdot \\mathrm{poly}(\\la