\) Hankel matrix (§6.1, p. 26)","computation":"Hankel singularity reduces to a half-GCD computation of \\( O(k \\log^{2} k) \\) (Imported Theorem 6.3, p. 25); the constant-round instantiation evaluates a circuit of size \\( \\tilde O(k \\cdot \\mathrm{poly}(\\lambda)) \\) and constant depth assuming a PRG in \\( \\mathrm{NC}^{1} \\) (§6.1, p. 26)"},"construction_family":"polynomial_threshold_psi","correctness":null,"corruption_model":null,"decapsulation_cost":null,"decrypt_cost":{},"decrypt_pairings":"","decryption_failure":null,"encapsulation_cost":null,"exactness":null,"id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-BMRR-TAHE-DIFF","identifiable_abort":null,"key_size":null,"large_universe":null,"misuse_resistance":null,"multi_use_attributes":null,"noise_management":null,"nonce_generation":null,"nonce_requirement":null,"nonce_size":null,"normative_status":null,"object_type":null,"online":null,"output_compatibility":null,"packing":null,"paper_ids":["PSI-PAPER-2021-BMRR"],"paper_title":"Multi-Party Threshold Private Set Intersection with Sublinear Communication","paper_url":"https://eprint.iacr.org/2020/600","parallelizable":null,"plaintext_space":null,"policy_class":null,"post_quantum_mechanism":null,"preprocessing":null,"primitive":"multiparty threshold PSI","privacy_model":null,"proof_model":null,"properties":{"adversary":["semi_honest"],"adversary_scope":"semi-honest environment corrupting any proper subset of the parties (§2.2, p. 5; Theorem 7.1, p. 28)","corruption_threshold":"semi-honest corruption of up to \\( n - 1 \\) of n parties (Theorem 7.1, p. 28)","output":["threshold"],"output_recipients":"every party receives I if \\( |(S_1 \\cup \\dots \\cup S_n) \\setminus I| \\le T \\), otherwise ⊥ (Figure 2, p. 6; Figure 9, p. 30)","parties":"multiparty","rounds":"\\( O(1) \\) when F_SingTest is realized by a jointly generated garbled circuit; \\( O(T \\log^{2} T) \\) with the homomorphic-evaluation instantiation (§6.1, p. 26; Corollary 7.2, p. 28)","security_model":["standard_model"],"set_size_regime":"balanced","setup":"n-out-of-n threshold additively homomorphic encryption with distributed setup; a prime \\( q > T(T + 1)(p - 1) 2^{\\kappa} \\) for the sparsity test (Theorem 6.5, p. 27); star network with central party P1 (§2.3, p. 6)","technique":["additively_homomorphic_encryption","garbled_circuits","polynomial_sparsity_test"]},"quantum_security":null,"query_communication":null,"resilience":null,"response_communication":null,"robustness":null,"security_mode":"computational","security_model":"UC, semi-honest, up to \\( n - 1 \\) corruptions; Theorem 6.5 in the F_SingTest-hybrid model and Theorem 7.1 in the F_CTest-diff-hybrid model (pp. 27-28)","security_notion":"multiparty threshold PSI, functionality F_TPSI-diff","server_model":null,"server_work":null,"setup_model":null,"signer_model":null,"signing_cost":null,"signing_rounds":null,"sizes":{},"statefulness":null,"summary":"The TAHE instantiation of Corollary 7.2 (p. 28), realizing PSI-CONTRIB-2021-BMRR-TAHE-THRESHOLD-PSI for F_TPSI-diff as defined in PSI-CONTRIB-2021-BMRR-FUNCTIONALITIES.","supported_gates":null,"tag_size":null,"threshold_policy":null,"transform":null,"update_model":null,"verification_cost":null,"work_id":"PSI-PAPER-2021-BMRR","year":2021},{"adaptive_security":null,"api_style":null,"associated_data":null,"assumption_family":"lattice","assumption_id":"PSI-ASSUMPTION-THRESHOLD-FHE-WITH-DISTRIBUTED-SETUP-FROM-CIRCULAR-SECURE-LWE-WITH-THRESHOLD-ADDITIVELY-HOMOMORPHIC-ENCRYPTION","assumption_name":"Threshold FHE with distributed setup from circular-secure LWE, with threshold additively homomorphic encryption","authors":["Saikrishna Badrinarayanan","Peihan Miao","Srinivasan Raghuraman","Peter Rindal"],"base_signature":null,"block_size":null,"bootstrapping":null,"capabilities":["sublinear-in-set-size","star-network"],"ciphertext_security":null,"circuit_class":null,"claim_ids":["PSI-CONTRIB-2021-BMRR-TFHE-UPPER-BOUND","PSI-CONTRIB-2021-BMRR-FUNCTIONALITIES"],"client_storage":null