2\\phi \\) bits, with \\( \\lambda = 40 \\) and \\( \\phi = 256 \\) (Table 1, p. 4)"},"construction_family":"key_agreement_polynomial_encoding","correctness":null,"corruption_model":null,"decapsulation_cost":null,"decrypt_cost":{},"decrypt_pairings":"","decryption_failure":null,"encapsulation_cost":null,"exactness":null,"id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-RT-SH-V2","identifiable_abort":null,"key_size":null,"large_universe":null,"misuse_resistance":null,"multi_use_attributes":null,"noise_management":null,"nonce_generation":null,"nonce_requirement":null,"nonce_size":null,"normative_status":null,"object_type":null,"online":null,"output_compatibility":null,"packing":null,"paper_ids":["PSI-PAPER-2021-RT"],"paper_title":"Compact and Malicious Private Set Intersection for Small Sets","paper_url":"https://eprint.iacr.org/2021/1159","parallelizable":null,"plaintext_space":null,"policy_class":null,"post_quantum_mechanism":null,"preprocessing":null,"primitive":"two-party PSI","privacy_model":null,"proof_model":null,"properties":{"adversary":["semi_honest"],"adversary_scope":"semi-honest sender and receiver (Appendix A.2 and Lemma 13, pp. 26-27)","output":["intersection"],"output_recipients":"the receiver only (Figure 6, step 7, p. 26)","parties":"two_party","rounds":"three messages \\( m \\), \\( P \\), \\( K \\) (Figure 6, p. 26)","security_model":["random_oracle_model"],"set_size_regime":"balanced","setup":"no ideal permutation; the receiver fixes \\( P(0) \\) to a random \\( R \\), assuming 0 is not a valid item; hashed Diffie-Hellman with elligator encoding (Appendix A.2, p. 26; §3.2, pp. 8-9)","technique":["key_agreement"]},"quantum_security":null,"query_communication":null,"resilience":null,"response_communication":null,"robustness":null,"security_mode":"computational","security_model":"semi-honest; non-malleable key agreement with pseudorandom second messages, which for hashed Diffie-Hellman is the oracle Diffie-Hellman assumption (Lemma 13, p. 27; §3.2, p. 9; Table 1, p. 4)","security_notion":"PSI with output to the receiver","server_model":null,"server_work":null,"setup_model":null,"signer_model":null,"signing_cost":null,"signing_rounds":null,"sizes":{},"statefulness":null,"summary":"The receiver encodes its key-agreement responses directly as \\( P(y_i) \\) and adds the point \\( P(0) = R \\), which lets the simulator program one evaluation at a time by solving for \\( R \\) (Appendix A.2, p. 26). The mechanism is PSI-CONTRIB-2021-RT-SEMI-HONEST-DH-COMMUNICATION.","supported_gates":null,"tag_size":null,"threshold_policy":null,"transform":null,"update_model":null,"verification_cost":null,"work_id":"PSI-PAPER-2021-RT","year":2021},{"adaptive_security":null,"api_style":null,"associated_data":null,"assumption_family":"idealized_model","assumption_id":"PSI-ASSUMPTION-RANDOM-ORACLES-IN-THE-OPPRF-AND-GENERIC-TWO-PARTY-COMPUTATION-HYBRID-MODELS-SILVER-FOR-SILENT-OT-AND-VOLE","assumption_name":"Random oracles, in the OPPRF and generic two-party computation hybrid models; Silver for silent OT and VOLE","authors":["Srinivasan Raghuraman","Peter Rindal"],"base_signature":null,"block_size":null,"bootstrapping":null,"capabilities":["secret-shared-output"],"ciphertext_security":null,"circuit_class":null,"claim_ids":["PSI-CONTRIB-2022-RR-TRIANGULATION-OKVS","PSI-CONTRIB-2021-RS-CIRCUIT-PSI"],"client_storage":null,"communication":null,"complexity":{"communication":"\\( 931n \\) and \\( 921n \\) bits for \\( n = 2^{16} \\) and \\( 2^{20} \\); asymptotically \\( O(n\\ell) \\) (Table 2, p. 25)","computation":"not stated beyond the measurements; the OKVS encodes in \\( O(m + g^{2}) \\) after linear-time triangulation (§2, p. 6)","reported_measurement":"1,112 ms and 15,557 ms for \\( n = 2^{16} \\) and \\( 2^{20} \\), on an Intel i7 9750H laptop over a local network of about 1 Gbps (Table 2, p. 25; §5, p. 23)"},"construction_family":"opprf_cuckoo_circuit","correctness":null,"corruption_model":null,"decapsulation_cost":null,"decrypt_cost":{},"decrypt_pairings":"","decryption_failure":null,"encapsulation_cost":null,"exactness":null,"id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2022-RR-CIRCUIT","identifiable_abort":null,"key_size":null,"large_universe":null,"misuse_resistance":null,"multi_use_attributes":null,"noise_management":null,"nonce_generation":null,"nonce_requirement":null,"nonce_size":null,"normative_status":null,"object_type":null,"online":null,"output_compatibility":null,"packing":null,"paper_ids":["PSI-PAPER-2022-RR","PSI-PAPER-2021-RS"],"paper_title":"Blazing Fast PSI from Improved OKVS and Subfield VOLE","paper_url":"https://eprint.iacr.org/2022/320","parallelizable":null,"plaintext_space":null,"policy_class":null,"post_quantum_mechanism":null,"preprocessing":null,"primitive":"circuit-PSI","privacy_model":null,"proof_model":null,"properties":{"adversary":["semi_honest"],"adversary_scope":"semi-honest, as in the circuit-PSI of VOLE-PSI that the paper uses (§4, p. 23; Table 2, p. 25)","output":["circuit"],"output_recipients":"both parties receive secret shares, as in the circuit-PSI of VOLE-PSI (§1, p. 2; §4, p. 23)","parties":"two_party","rounds":"not_reported","security_model":["random_oracle_model"],"set_size_regime":"balanced","setup":"the circuit-PSI protocol of PSI-PAPER-2021-RS with the OKVS in its doubly oblivious form (Figure 1, step 5, p. 7; Theorem 2, p. 31; §4, p. 23) and Silver (Table 2, p. 25)","technique":["opprf","okvs","vole","cuckoo_hashing"]},"quantum_security":null,"query_communication":null,"resilience":null,"response_communication":null,"robustness":null,"security_mode":"computational","security_model":"semi-honest two-party, by reference to the circuit-PSI of PSI-PAPER-2021-RS (§4, p. 23)","security_notion":"circuit-PSI with secret-shared output","server_model":null,"server_work":null,"setup_model":null,"signer_model":null,"signing_cost":null,"signing_rounds":null,"sizes":{},"statefulness":null,"summary":"The row applies PSI-CONTRIB-2022-RR-TRIANGULATION-OKVS, in the doubly oblivious form that circuit PSI needs, to the protocol of PSI-CONTRIB-2021-RS-CIRCUIT-PSI, with Silver for the remaining correlations (§4, p. 23; Table 2, p. 25).","supported_gates":null,"tag_size":null,"threshold_policy":null,"transform":null,"update_model":null,"verification_cost":null,"work_id":"PSI-PAPER-2022-RR","year":2022},{"adaptive_security":null,"api_style":null,"associated_data":null,"assumption_family":"idealized_model","assumption_id":"PSI-ASSUMPTION-RANDOM-ORACLES-IN-THE-SUBFIELD-VOLE-HYBRID-MODEL-VOLE-FOLLOWING-COUTEAU-RINDAL-RAGHURAMAN-2021-AND-BOYLE-ET-AL-2019","assumption_name":"Random oracles, in the subfield-VOLE hybrid model; VOLE following Couteau-Rindal-Raghuraman 2021 and Boyle et al. 2019","authors":["Srinivasan Raghuraman","Peter Rindal"],"base_signature":null,"block_size":null,"bootstrapping":null,"capabilities":["multi-threaded"],"ciphertext_security":null,"circuit_class":null,"claim_ids":["PSI-CONTRIB-2022-RR-TRIANGULATION-OKVS","PSI-CONTRIB-2021-RS-VOLE-OPRF"],"client_storage":null,"communication":null,"complexity":{"communication":"\\( 1.3\\kappa n_x + (\\lambda + \\log(n_x n_y)) n_y + 2^{14.5} \\kappa \\) bits; \\( 241n \\), \\( 251n \\), and \\( 260n \\) bits for \\( n = 2^{16}, 2^{20}, 2^{24} \\) (Table 2, p. 25)","computation":"OKVS encoding in \\( O(m + g^{2}) \\) after linear-time triangulation (§2, p. 6); 143 ms to encode \\( 2^{20} \\) items with clusters of \\( 2^{14} \\) (Table 1, p. 25)","reported_measurement":"51 ms, 369 ms, and 6,987 ms for \\( n = 2^{16}, 2^{20}, 2^{24} \\) on one thread, and 49 ms, 163 ms, and 3,145 ms with 4 threads, on an Intel i7 9750H laptop with 16 GB RAM over a local network of about 1 Gbps (Table 2, p. 25; §5, p. 23)"},"construction_family":"vole_okvs_oprf","correctness":null,"corruption_model":null,"decapsulation_cost":null,"decrypt_cost":{},"decrypt_pairings":"","decryption_failure":null,"encapsulation_cost":null,"exactness":null,"id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2022-RR-FAST","identifiable_abort":null,"key_size":null,"large_universe":null,