["threshold"],"output_recipients":"the parties learn the intersection if it has at least \\( n - t \\) elements, otherwise \\( \\bot \\) (abstract and §1, p. 1); the cardinality test outputs \\( \\ell \\)-out-of-\\( \\ell \\) secret shares (Figure 9, p. 11)","parties":"multiparty","rounds":"not_reported","security_model":"not_reported","set_size_regime":"balanced","setup":"pairwise authenticated private channels and a broadcast channel of unit cost (§2.1, p. 4); \\( \\epsilon \\) public random functions into \\( t \\) buckets, replaceable by PRFs with a public key (footnote 4, p. 3); inner multiparty cardinality test of Branco, Döttling, and Pu with generic secure computation (§4.1, p. 16)","technique":["secret_sharing","simple_hashing","additively_homomorphic_encryption"]},"quantum_security":null,"query_communication":null,"resilience":null,"response_communication":null,"robustness":null,"security_mode":"computational","security_model":"standalone, static passive adversary corrupting all but one party; Theorems 7-8 in hybrid models with ideal functionalities (pp. 15-16); correctness except with probability \\( 2^{-\\epsilon} \\) (Theorem 6, p. 14)","security_notion":"multiparty threshold PSI (intersection of at least \\( n - t \\) elements)","server_model":null,"server_work":null,"setup_model":null,"signer_model":null,"signing_cost":null,"signing_rounds":null,"sizes":{},"statefulness":null,"summary":"The \\( \\ell \\)-party protocol of Corollary 6 (p. 16): the cardinality-test compiler of PSI-CONTRIB-2023-GS-PICT-COMPILER applied to the Branco-Döttling-Pu test, then the intersection step of PSI-PAPER-2019-GS. It realizes PSI-CONTRIB-2023-GS-MULTIPARTY-QUASILINEAR.","supported_gates":null,"tag_size":null,"threshold_policy":null,"transform":null,"update_model":null,"verification_cost":null,"work_id":"PSI-PAPER-2023-GS","year":2023},{"adaptive_security":null,"api_style":null,"associated_data":null,"assumption_family":"generic","assumption_id":"PSI-ASSUMPTION-OBLIVIOUS