:"RS21 §1.3 (p. 5); §4 (pp. 19-20); §7.1 (p. 26), IACR ePrint 2021/266, PDF dated 2024-08-08","evidenceUrl":"https://eprint.iacr.org/2021/266","id":"PSI-REL-B2410EA9D47C56","note":"VOLE-PSI shows that the \\( 2\\kappa \\)-bit sender values required by the PaXoS-PSI analysis can be reduced to κ bits by extracting only non-colliding OPRF queries.","resultId":"PSI-CONTRIB-2020-PRTY-MALICIOUS-PAXOS-PSI","reviewStatus":"fulltext_checked","source":"PSI-CONTRIB-2020-PRTY-MALICIOUS-PAXOS-PSI","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2021-RS-SHORT-OPRF-OUTPUTS","type":"ANALYZES"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-B2554E4CCCCA60","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-RT-MAL","target":"PSI-PAPER-2021-RT","type":"DESCRIBED_IN"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-B261CBD39CCF91","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2017-KMPRT-3PARTY","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2017-KMPRT-OPPRF","type":"SUPPORTED_BY_CLAIM"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-B37EB085F8A4F6","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2017-CLR","target":"PSI-PAPER-2017-CLR","type":"DESCRIBED_IN"},{"evidenceLocator":"NTY §2.0.4 (p. 5), Protocols 3.1 and 3.3 (pp. 6, 8), proof of Theorem 3.2 (p. 7), IACR ePrint 2021/1221, PDF dated 2021-09-17","evidenceUrl":"https://eprint.iacr.org/2021/1221","id":"PSI-REL-B39E80FFC99C37","note":"P1 and the other senders encode their items with PRF values in OKVSs, whose obliviousness the simulation uses to replace them with random encodings.","resultId":"PSI-CONTRIB-2021-GPRTY-OKVS","reviewStatus":"fulltext_checked","source":"PSI-CONTRIB-2021-GPRTY-OKVS","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2021-NTY-MALICIOUS-NO-COLLUSION","type":"BUILDS_ON_MECHANISM"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-B642A632D55703","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2020-ION-ROT","target