s the plaintext modulus of the item length used by CLR17 with extension-field SIMD slots, making arbitrary-length (80-bit hashed) items efficient where CLR17 was practically limited to 32 bits.","resultId":"PSI-CONTRIB-2017-CLR-FHE-SUBLINEAR-COMMUNICATION","reviewStatus":"fulltext_checked","source":"PSI-CONTRIB-2017-CLR-FHE-SUBLINEAR-COMMUNICATION","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2018-CHLR-LONG-ITEMS","type":"IMPROVES_EFFICIENCY"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-CCE94BB89441A2","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2004-FNP-MULTIPARTY","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2004-FNP-MULTIPARTY-OPE","type":"SUPPORTED_BY_CLAIM"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-CD0BF54BB3CEA1","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2017-KMPRT-SH","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2017-KMPRT-OPPRF","type":"SUPPORTED_BY_CLAIM"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-CDC4247FFF9606","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2020-PRTY-SH","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2020-PRTY-GARBLED-CUCKOO","type":"SUPPORTED_BY_CLAIM"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-CDDE1B05AA60C2","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2004-FNP-MAL-SERVER","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2004-FNP-MALICIOUS-OPE","type":"SUPPORTED_BY_CLAIM"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-CE1E9E02F27DC6","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2020-PRTY-SH","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2020-PRTY-PAXOS","type":"SUPPORTED_BY_CLAIM"},{"evidenceLocator":"VCE §5.3.3 (pp. 11-12), Table 3 (p. 13), Appendix B.2 (p. 18), IACR ePrint 2023/1777, PDF dated 2023-11-16","evidenceUrl":"https://eprint.iacr.org/2023/1777","id":"PSI-REL-CE3EB6B9CD684C","note":"VCE count tk OPPRFs at the leader and k per assistant for the ZeroXOR step of NTY, 3.5tk OTs in total, and describe it as outperforming the protocols of Kolesnikov et al., Ben-Efraim et al., and Chandran et al.","resultId":"PSI-CONTRIB-2021-NTY-MALICIOUS-THRESHOLD-CALIBRATED","reviewStatus":"fulltext_checked","source":"PSI-CONTRIB-2021-NTY-MALICIOUS-THRESHOLD-CALIBRATED","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2024-VCE-ANALYTICAL-COST-COMPARISON","type":"ANALYZES"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-CEA44044209B5E","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2004-FNP-SH","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2004-FNP-BALANCED-ALLOCATION-HASHING","type":"SUPPORTED_BY_CLAIM"},{"evidenceLocator":"CHLR18 §1.3 (p. 3), §7.2 (p. 16), §7.3 (pp. 17-18), Theorem 3 (p. 25), IACR ePrint 2018/787, PDF dated 2018-08-27","evidenceUrl":"https://eprint.iacr.org/2018/787","id":"PSI-REL-CFBA1C1578FE78","note":"CHLR18 restricts what a malicious sender can do in FHE-based unbalanced PSI from forcing the intersection to be the receiver's full set, as in CLR17, to X ∩ Y ∩ leakage(Y), under an H-limited FHE assumption.","resultId":"PSI-CONTRIB-2017-CLR-FHE-SUBLINEAR-COMMUNICATION","reviewStatus":"fulltext_checked","source":"PSI-CONTRIB-2017-CLR-FHE-SUBLINEAR-COMMUNICATION","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2018-CHLR-LEAKY-MALICIOUS-SENDER","type":"HARDENS"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-D073D26D886B39","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2004-FNP-SH","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2004-FNP-OPE-PSI","type":"SUPPORTED_BY_CLAIM"},{"evidenceLocator":"KMPRT §3.1 (pp. 4-5), §3.4 (p. 7), §4 (p. 9), IACR ePrint 2017/799, PDF dated 2017-08-24","evidenceUrl":"https://eprint.iacr.org/2017/799","id":"PSI-REL-D0BBC5F91DCC6A","note":"KMPRT build every OPPRF from the KKRT batched OPRF, one OPRF instance per bin plus a sender hint, and inherit its related-key and leakage relaxations.","resultId":"PSI-CONTRIB-2016-KKRT-BATCHED-OPRF","reviewStatus":"fulltext_checked","source":"PSI-CONTRIB-2016-KKRT-BATCHED-OPRF","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2017-KMPRT-OPPRF","type":"BUILDS_ON_MECHANISM"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-D1A6C04E9AD47D","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2019-PSTY-ADVANCED","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2019-PSTY-LINEAR-COMMUNICATION","type":"SUPPORTED_BY_CLAIM"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-D23BFA8662B48F","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-PAPER-2018-PSZ","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2018-PSZ-HASHING-PARAMETERS","type":"HAS_RESULT"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-D29B119D5404FB","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-PAPER-2018-CHLR","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2018-CHLR-LABELED-PSI","type":"HAS_RESULT"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-D3E3B0265FABD9","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"scheme_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2017-KMPRT-3PARTY","target":"PSI-ASSUMPTION-PRF-AND-RANDOM-ORACLE-WITH-THE-OPPRF-INSTANTIATED-FROM-THE-KKRT-BATCHED-OPRF","type":"RELIES_ON"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-D434EA34063E7E","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-NTY-ARBITRARY-COLLUSION","target":"PSI-PAPER-2021-NTY","type":"DESCRIBED_IN"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-D440B9F66A4C82","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2017-RR-CCS-EC-ROM","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2017-RR-CCS-ENCODE-COMMIT","type":"SUPPORTED_BY_CLAIM"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-D520C3F689627C","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"scheme_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2020-ION-DDH","target":"PSI-ASSUMPTION-DDH-AND-CPA-SECURE-ADDITIVELY-HOMOMORPHIC-ENCRYPTION-RANDOM-ORACLE-MODEL-PAILLIER-WITH-DAMG-RD-JURIK-IN-DEPLOYMENT","type":"RELIES_ON"},{"evidenceLocator":"RS21 §1.4 (p. 6); §6 (pp. 22-23); Table 4 (p. 29), IACR ePrint 2021/266, PDF dated 2024-08-08","evidenceUrl":"https://eprint.iacr.org/2021/266","id":"PSI-REL-D574B7ABCCB8A4","note":"VOLE-PSI's circuit-PSI keeps the PSTY19 protocol and replaces its polynomial-based OPPRF with one built from the VOLE OPRF and XoPaXoS; for \\( 2^{20} \\) items it runs in 23.3 s against 72.0 s at 5 Gbps with IKNP-based GMW.","resultId":"PSI-CONTRIB-2019-PSTY-LINEAR-COMMUNICATION","reviewStatus":"fulltext_checked","source":"PSI-CONTRIB-2019-PSTY-LINEAR-COMMUNICATION","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2021-RS-CIRCUIT-PSI","type":"IMPROVES_EFFICIENCY"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-D602B8C9D9CF5A","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-PAPER-2017-KMPRT","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2017-KMPRT-AUGMENTED-ZERO-SHARING","type":"HAS_RESULT"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-D71164527456C2","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-NTY-NO-COLLUSION","target":"PSI-PAPER-2021-NTY","type":"DESCRIBED_IN"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-D734B5F88B72AA","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"scheme_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2023-GS-TWO-PARTY","target":"PSI-ASSUMPTION-OBLIVIOUS-TRANSFER-OR-ADDITIVELY-HOMOMORPHIC-ENCRYPTION-ANY-ASSUMPTION-IMPLYING-SECURE-COMPUTATION","type":"RELIES_ON"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-D74E2465FB9B8F","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2004-FNP-MAL-CLIENT","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2004-FNP-MALICIOUS-OPE","type":"SUPPORTED_BY_CLAIM"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-D7DC2F4823B2A9","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2019-PSTY-BASIC","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2019-PSTY-BATCHED-OPPRF","type":"SUPPORTED_BY_CLAIM"},{"evidenceLocator":"CHLR18 §1.3 (p. 3) and §5.1 (pp. 11-12), IACR ePrint 2018/787, PDF dated 2018-08-27","evidenceUrl":"https://eprint.iacr.org/2018/787","id":"PSI-REL-D86F7502610F13","note":"CHLR18 extends the CLR17 protocol to labeled PSI: the sender additionally evaluates a label-interpolation polynomial per bin, keeping communication sublinear in the sender's set.","resultId":"PSI-CONTRIB-2017-CLR-FHE-SUBLINEAR-COMMUNICATION","reviewStatus":"fulltext_checked","source":"PSI-CONTRIB-2017-CLR-FHE-SUBLINEAR-COMMUNICATION","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2018-CHLR-LABELED-PSI","type":"EXTENDS"},{"evidenceLocator":"GS23 §1.2 (p. 2) and §3.1 (p. 10), IACR ePrint 2023/919, PDF dated 2023-06-12","evidenceUrl":"https://eprint.iacr.org/2023/919","id":"PSI-REL-D8748195710498","note":"GS23 follows the GS19 split into a cardinality test and an intersection step, and instantiates the inner two-party test of its compiler with the GS19 cardinality test, adapted to secret-shared output and run at logarithmic thresholds.","resultId":"PSI-CONTRIB-2019-GS-AHE-THRESHOLD-PSI","reviewStatus":"fulltext_checked","source":"PSI-CONTRIB-2019-GS-AHE-THRESHOLD-PSI","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2023-GS-PICT-COMPILER","type":"BUILDS_ON_MECHANISM"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-D8A66D1244E786","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-NTY-ARBITRARY-COLLUSION","target":"PSI-PAPER-2017-KMPRT","type":"DESCRIBED_IN"},{"evidenceLocator":"NTY §2 (pp. 4-5), Protocol 4.2 (p. 10), §5 (p. 11), IACR ePrint 2021/1221, PDF dated 2021-09-17","evidenceUrl":"https://eprint.iacr.org/2021/1221","id":"PSI-REL-D9031CE7805242","note":"NTY take the OPPRF definitions almost verbatim from KMPRT and run an OPPRF from each of t parties to P_n inside ZeroXOR.","resultId":"PSI-CONTRIB-2017-KMPRT-OPPRF","reviewStatus":"fulltext_checked","source":"PSI-CONTRIB-2017-KMPRT-OPPRF","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2021-NTY-MALICIOUS-THRESHOLD-CALIBRATED","type":"BUILDS_ON_MECHANISM"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-D9A9832C02564F","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2010-DT-FIG3","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2010-DT-LINEAR-APSI","type":"SUPPORTED_BY_CLAIM"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-DA64E354B0D9BE","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-PAPER-2020-PRTY","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2020-PRTY-MALICIOUS-PAXOS-PSI","type":"HAS_RESULT"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-DABFF319A31613","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-PAPER-2019-PSTY","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2019-PSTY-BATCHED-OPPRF","type":"HAS_RESULT"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-DB1F0DA6F08D29","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-GPRTY-MAL-STAR","target":"PSI-PAPER-2021-GPRTY","type":"DESCRIBED_IN"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-DB3E20D69EBAC0","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-NTY-NO-COLLUSION","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2021-NTY-MALICIOUS-NO-COLLUSION","type":"SUPPORTED_BY_CLAIM"},{"evidenceLocator":"PSWW18 abstract (p. 1), §1.4 (p. 5), and §6.2 (pp. 21-22), IACR ePrint 2018/120, PDF dated 2019-01-24","evidenceUrl":"https://eprint.iacr.org/2018/120","id":"PSI-REL-DC005BBC68544C","note":"Mirror cuckoo hashing reduces the comparisons of circuit-based PSI from the \\( O(n \\log n) \\) of the sort-compare-shuffle circuit to \\( \\omega(n) \\).","resultId":"PSI-CONTRIB-2012-HEK-SORT-COMPARE-SHUFFLE","reviewStatus":"fulltext_checked","source":"PSI-CONTRIB-2012-HEK-SORT-COMPARE-SHUFFLE","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2018-PSWW-ALMOST-LINEAR-CIRCUIT","type":"IMPROVES_EFFICIENCY"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-DC24661E80FE2A","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2023-GS-MULTIPARTY","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2023-GS-PICT-COMPILER","type":"SUPPORTED_BY_CLAIM"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-DC4AF7618A53D3","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-PAPER-1999-HFH","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-1999-HFH-DH-PREFERENCE-MATCHING","type":"HAS_RESULT"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-DD55CA24721F33","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2019-KRSSW-GC","target":"PSI-PAPER-2019-KRSSW","type":"DESCRIBED_IN"},{"evidenceLocator":"GPRTY21 §1.1 (p. 3); §2.1-2.3 (pp. 5-6), IACR ePrint 2021/883, PDF dated 2021-11-30","evidenceUrl":"https://eprint.iacr.org/2021/883","id":"PSI-REL-DF0EFAA989A483","note":"The OKVS definition generalizes PaXoS from binary to linear and other key-value encodings and makes obliviousness explicit; a binary OKVS is a PaXoS.","resultId":"PSI-CONTRIB-2020-PRTY-PAXOS","reviewStatus":"fulltext_checked","source":"PSI-CONTRIB-2020-PRTY-PAXOS","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2021-GPRTY-OKVS","type":"GENERALIZES"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-E0A1A0C5960639","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2017-RR-CCS-EC-ROM","target":"PSI-PAPER-2017-RR-CCS","type":"DESCRIBED_IN"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-E11696FDE933A6","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-CONG","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2021-CONG-PATERSON-STOCKMEYER","type":"SUPPORTED_BY_CLAIM"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-E17848EC6CD828","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-PAPER-2004-FNP","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2004-FNP-CARDINALITY-THRESHOLD","type":"HAS_RESULT"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-E1978DBB4E2947","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-BMRR-AHE-TWO-PARTY","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2019-GS-AHE-THRESHOLD-PSI","type":"SUPPORTED_BY_CLAIM"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-E38409EC829384","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2018-CHLR","target":"PSI-PAPER-2018-CHLR","type":"DESCRIBED_IN"},{"evidenceLocat