int 2020/600, PDF dated 2021-02-25","evidenceUrl":"https://eprint.iacr.org/2020/600","id":"PSI-REL-E80F7DCBAEF828","note":"BMRR generalize the two-party threshold PSI functionality of GS19 to two multiparty functionalities that coincide for two parties.","resultId":"PSI-CONTRIB-2019-GS-AHE-THRESHOLD-PSI","reviewStatus":"fulltext_checked","source":"PSI-CONTRIB-2019-GS-AHE-THRESHOLD-PSI","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2021-BMRR-FUNCTIONALITIES","type":"GENERALIZES"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-E8579D423BF124","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2020-ION-DDH","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2020-ION-DDH-INTERSECTION-SUM","type":"SUPPORTED_BY_CLAIM"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-E89917946A7E50","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"scheme_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2004-FNP-CARDINALITY","target":"PSI-ASSUMPTION-SEMANTIC-SECURITY-OF-AN-ADDITIVELY-HOMOMORPHIC-ENCRYPTION-SCHEME-PAILLIER-NAMED-AS-AN-INSTANCE","type":"RELIES_ON"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-E916112EC59937","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2004-FNP-MAL-CLIENT","target":"PSI-PAPER-2004-FNP","type":"DESCRIBED_IN"},{"evidenceLocator":"CMGD21 §1.2 (p. 3) and §3.1 (pp. 7-8), IACR ePrint 2021/1116, PDF dated 2021-11-14","evidenceUrl":"https://eprint.iacr.org/2021/1116","id":"PSI-REL-E9579E75D343E2","note":"CMGD21 replaces computing all powers up to the partition size, as in the CLR17 framework retained by CHLR18, with Paterson-Stockmeyer evaluation, reducing non-scalar multiplications per bin from linear to \\( O(\\sqrt{B}) \\).","resultId":"PSI-CONTRIB-2017-CLR-FHE-SUBLINEAR-COMMUNICATION","reviewStatus":"fulltext_checked","source":"PSI-CONTRIB-2017-CLR-FHE-SUBLINEAR-COMMUNICATION","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2021-CONG-PATERSON-STOCKMEYER","type":"IMPROVES_EFFICIENCY"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-EA925B91DF5519","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2022-RR-MAL","target":"PSI-PAPER-2022-RR","type":"DESCRIBED_IN"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-EAAB075E71CC49","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2018-CHLR-LABELED","target":"PSI-PAPER-2017-CLR","type":"DESCRIBED_IN"},{"evidenceLocator":"NTY §2.0.4 (p. 5), Protocol 4.4 (p. 10), §5 (p. 11), IACR ePrint 2021/1221, PDF dated 2021-09-17","evidenceUrl":"https://eprint.iacr.org/2021/1221","id":"PSI-REL-EAD3970580F753","note":"Each client sends the pivot a single OKVS encoding its items instead of running pairwise OPPRFs, using the OKVS definition of Garimella et al. and PaXoS as the instance they prove oblivious.","resultId":"PSI-CONTRIB-2021-GPRTY-OKVS","reviewStatus":"fulltext_checked","source":"PSI-CONTRIB-2021-GPRTY-OKVS","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2021-NTY-MALICIOUS-THRESHOLD-CALIBRATED","type":"BUILDS_ON_MECHANISM"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-EAE455543FE3BD","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-RS-MAL","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2021-RS-VOLE-OPRF","type":"SUPPORTED_BY_CLAIM"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-EB330AA9E4BD38","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-PAPER-2021-CONG","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2021-CONG-POSTAGE-STAMP-BASES","type":"HAS_RESULT"},{"evidenceLocator":"","evidenceUrl":"","id":"PSI-REL-EB54F1DD25536D","note":"","resultId":null,"reviewStatus":"source_declared","source":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2020-PRTY-MAL","target":"PSI-CONTRIB-2020-PRTY-GARBLED-CUCKOO","type":"SUPPORTED_BY_CLAIM"},{"evidenceLocator":"GPRTY21 §6.3 (p. 19); §8.2 (p. 23); Table 1 (p. 24), IACR ePrint 2021/883, PDF dated 2021-11-30","evidenceUrl":"https://eprint.iacr.org/2021/883","id":"PSI-REL-EB6E1EF5A2618C","note":"Used as the binary OKVS of PaXoS-PSI, the three-hash table reduces the malicious protocol's communication 1.6