er bin and partition, with collision-aware insertion; updates use a fresh random nonce per label (§4.2, pp. 13-14)"},{"dimension":"setup","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-CONG.md","id":"PSI-PROP-98B4B3922492BA","review_status":"fulltext_checked","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-CONG","value":"the sender samples the OPRF key and pre-processes its OPRF-processed set offline; the precomputation is updatable (§3, p. 6; §4.2, p. 13); OMGDH-based OPRF over the FourQ curve with a random-oracle hash to the curve (§3.1, p. 12)"},{"dimension":"capability_tag","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2020-PRTY-SH.md","id":"PSI-PROP-98C91357C1DD89","review_status":"scheme_declared","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2020-PRTY-SH","value":"linear-communication"},{"dimension":"construction_family","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-CONG.md","id":"PSI-PROP-98D934F911109E","review_status":"fulltext_checked","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-CONG","value":"oprf_fhe_polynomial_evaluation_cuckoo_hashing"},{"dimension":"parties","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-BMRR-TFHE-INT.md","id":"PSI-PROP-994326F2696CE5","review_status":"fulltext_checked","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-BMRR-TFHE-INT","value":"multiparty"},{"dimension":"output_recipients","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-RS-MAL.md","id":"PSI-PROP-999FA2894F8A08","review_status":"fulltext_checked","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-RS-MAL","value":"receiver only (Figure 5, p. 37; Figure 6, step 4, p. 37)"},{"dimension":"technique","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-BMRR-TFHE-DIFF.md","id":"PSI-PROP-9A0DB287A0A12D","review_status":"fulltext_checked","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-BMRR-TFHE-DIFF","value":"threshold_fhe"},{"dimension":"adversary","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2017-KMPRT-3PARTY.md","id":"PSI-PROP-9ABE0CAB600641","review_status":"fulltext_checked","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2017-KMPRT-3PARTY","value":"semi_honest"},{"dimension":"rounds","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-GPRTY-MAL-3HGCT.md","id":"PSI-PROP-9AEB7E4B28AAFD","review_status":"fulltext_checked","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-GPRTY-MAL-3HGCT","value":"not_reported"},{"dimension":"set_size_regime","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2012-HEK-SCS-HE.md","id":"PSI-PROP-9B0A6ABB9463A3","review_status":"fulltext_checked","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2012-HEK-SCS-HE","value":"balanced"},{"dimension":"construction_family","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-NTY-ARBITRARY-COLLUSION.md","id":"PSI-PROP-9B139895743464","review_status":"fulltext_checked","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-NTY-ARBITRARY-COLLUSION","value":"okvs_zeroxor"},{"dimension":"corruption_threshold","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-NTY-NO-COLLUSION.md","id":"PSI-PROP-9B5DAD44F6320B","review_status":"fulltext_checked","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-NTY-NO-COLLUSION","value":"no collusion, \\( t \\le 1 \\) (§1.2, p. 4); \\( t = 1 \\) (Table 1, p. 2); a collusion of two parties such as \\( P_1 \\) and \\( P_{n-1} \\) breaks the protocol (§3.2.1, p. 8)"},{"dimension":"construction_family","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2017-KMPRT-AUG.md","id":"PSI-PROP-9B6319CC2941C9","review_status":"fulltext_checked","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2017-KMPRT-AUG","value":"opprf_unconditional_zero_sharing"},{"dimension":"security_model","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2023-GS-MULTIPARTY.md","id":"PSI-PROP-9B6E3B068ED682","review_status":"fulltext_checked","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2023-GS-MULTIPARTY","value":"not_reported"},{"dimension":"technique","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2004-FNP-CARDINALITY.md","id":"PSI-PROP-9B7C8C0DF7A0AB","review_status":"fulltext_checked","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2004-FNP-CARDINALITY","value":"oblivious_polynomial_evaluation"},{"dimension":"setup","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-RS-SH.md","id":"PSI-PROP-9BCB01F52B6DCB","review_status":"fulltext_checked","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-RS-SH","value":"F_vole-hybrid with a random VOLE of length \\( m = 2.4n + d + \\lambda \\) over a field of about \\( 2^{\\kappa} \\) elements (Figure 1, p. 7; Figure 4, p. 36); the implementation uses LPN-based VOLE with iterative bootstrapping, part of which runs in a one-time, data-independent setup (§3.1, p. 14; §7.2, pp. 26-27); random oracles \\( H \\) and \\( H_F \\)"},{"dimension":"output","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-RS-CIRCUIT.md","id":"PSI-PROP-9BFA5A47C795FB","review_status":"fulltext_checked","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-RS-CIRCUIT","value":"circuit"},{"dimension":"setup","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-BMRR-TAHE-DIFF.md","id":"PSI-PROP-9BFBA95CC6A80B","review_status":"fulltext_checked","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-BMRR-TAHE-DIFF","value":"n-out-of-n threshold additively homomorphic encryption with distributed setup; a prime \\( q > T(T + 1)(p - 1) 2^{\\kappa} \\) for the sparsity test (Theorem 6.5, p. 27); star network with central party P1 (§2.3, p. 6)"},{"dimension":"set_size_regime","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2004-FNP-CARDINALITY.md","id":"PSI-PROP-9C21114A369C29","review_status":"fulltext_checked","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2004-FNP-CARDINALITY","value":"balanced"},{"dimension":"primitive","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2004-FNP-MAL-SERVER.md","id":"PSI-PROP-9CC382E9F8CBBE","review_status":"fulltext_checked","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2004-FNP-MAL-SERVER","value":"two-party PSI"},{"dimension":"parties","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2016-KKRT.md","id":"PSI-PROP-9CC3ECE30FE4A7","review_status":"fulltext_checked","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2016-KKRT","value":"two_party"},{"dimension":"capability_tag","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-NTY-NO-COLLUSION.md","id":"PSI-PROP-9E031D5A684DAF","review_status":"scheme_declared","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-NTY-NO-COLLUSION","value":"symmetric-key-primitives-only"},{"dimension":"rounds","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2020-PRTY-SH.md","id":"PSI-PROP-9ED872779DC8B3","review_status":"fulltext_checked","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2020-PRTY-SH","value":"not_reported"},{"dimension":"capability_tag","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2018-CHLR-LABELED.md","id":"PSI-PROP-9EE001035B6C55","review_status":"scheme_declared","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2018-CHLR-LABELED","value":"batched-keyword-pir"},{"dimension":"setup","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-RS-CIRCUIT.md","id":"PSI-PROP-9F0984FAEB6E76","review_status":"fulltext_checked","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-RS-CIRCUIT","value":"cuckoo hashing with expansion 1.27 and three hash functions, following Pinkas, Schneider, Tkachenko, and Yanai (§7.2, pp. 29-30); OPPRF from the VOLE-based OPRF, whose security uses random oracles, and XoPaXoS (Figure 8, p. 38); generic two-party computation for the comparison, implemented with GMW whose OTs come from IKNP or SilentOT (§7.2, p. 30)"},{"dimension":"capability_tag","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2022-RR-MAL.md","id":"PSI-PROP-9F572633DE80F1","review_status":"scheme_declared","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2022-RR-MAL","value":"multi-threaded"},{"dimension":"adversary_scope","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-RS-MAL.md","id":"PSI-PROP-9F7FF8D9CB6D2E","review_status":"fulltext_checked","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-RS-MAL","value":"malicious sender or receiver (Theorem 3.1, p. 16; Theorem 4.1, p. 20); a malicious receiver's effective set is bounded by \\( n' = O(n) \\) through the PaXoS size bound, and by \\( m \\) under the authors' Strong OKVS Extraction Conjecture (§2, pp. 11-12; Lemma 3.3, p. 18)"},{"dimension":"adversary_scope","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2019-PSTY-NO-STASH.md","id":"PSI-PROP-9F82CF7FB2ED0F","review_status":"fulltext_checked","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2019-PSTY-NO-STASH","value":"semi-honest P1 (receiver) and P2 (sender) (§2.1-2.2, p. 8)"},{"dimension":"parties","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-NTY-NO-COLLUSION.md","id":"PSI-PROP-9F8715B075835C","review_status":"fulltext_checked","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2021-NTY-NO-COLLUSION","value":"multiparty"},{"dimension":"output_recipients","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2019-GS-AHE.md","id":"PSI-PROP-9FC69515A4D171","review_status":"fulltext_checked","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2019-GS-AHE","value":"both parties receive the intersection if the symmetric difference is at most \\( 2t \\), otherwise ⊥ (Figure 6, p. 12)"},{"dimension":"capability_tag","evidence_ref":"knowledge/p