PSI-CONSTRUCTION-1999-HFH","value":"four messages, two in each direction (Appendix A, steps 1-4, p. 85)"},{"dimension":"construction_family","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2018-PSWW-2D.md","id":"PSI-PROP-A2F3E364A207A6","review_status":"fulltext_checked","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2018-PSWW-2D","value":"cuckoo_hashing_circuit_psi"},{"dimension":"adversary_scope","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2004-FNP-MAL-SERVER.md","id":"PSI-PROP-A3099FC9720311","review_status":"fulltext_checked","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2004-FNP-MAL-SERVER","value":"malicious server (Lemma 4, p. 12); the server's privacy is preserved as in the semi-honest protocol, and a malicious client is treated by a separate protocol (§5.2, p. 11; §5.1, p. 10)"},{"dimension":"rounds","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2004-FNP-MAL-CLIENT.md","id":"PSI-PROP-A30E9B244CE9C0","review_status":"fulltext_checked","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2004-FNP-MAL-CLIENT","value":"client sends L copies, server chooses \\( L/2 \\) to open, client opens them and sends the keys of the rest, server replies (Protocol PM-Malicious-Client, steps 1-4, p. 10)"},{"dimension":"technique","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2018-PSZ-OT.md","id":"PSI-PROP-A325AED5C4A114","review_status":"fulltext_checked","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2018-PSZ-OT","value":"cuckoo_hashing"},{"dimension":"output_recipients","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2020-PRTY-SH.md","id":"PSI-PROP-A360E0C8C98C23","review_status":"fulltext_checked","scope":"construction","subject_id":"PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2020-PRTY-SH","value":"receiver only (Figure 1, p. 6; Figure 3, step 4, p. 11)"},{"dimension":"adversary_scope","evidence_ref":"knowledge/primitives/psi/schemes/PSI-CONSTRUCTION-2022-RR-CIRCUIT.md","id":"PSI